  alt        the Upsilon_V that centres the EFE-quasi-Newtonian relation: 22.42 (scatter 0.330 dex)
  [PASS] 8a AGAINST INTEREST -- the dwarf sigma law does NOT close with a stellar-population M/L: centring the EFE-quasi-Newtonian relation needs Upsilon_V ~ 5-10, three times what old stellar populations give, and the observed dispersions sit ABOVE the prediction by ~0.2-0.3 dex at Upsilon_V = 2, on both footings.  This reproduces a known MOND tension for Milky Way dwarfs (Angus 2008), it is not new here   (canonical: centring Upsilon_V = 23.8 (scatter 0.325 dex); alt: centring Upsilon_V = 22.4 (scatter 0.330 dex))
  [PASS] 8b the split says where the trouble is: report MW and M31 separately, since the MW subsample is the more EFE-dominated and the more tidally disturbed   (MW: +0.641 dex (N=22, rms 0.440); M31: +0.294 dex (N=19); the three prescriptions bracket the data (Newtonian +0.789, EFE +0.363, isolated MOND +0.169 dex))

