  MW dwarfs: N = 22; the LMC's deep-MOND field at their typical distances is x_LMC = 0.008 - 0.070 in a_0 units
  the MW's own field at the same distances is x_MW = 0.095 (at 100 kpc): the LMC term is a 33% perturbation
  [PASS] 96 the LMC hemispheric test CANNOT be done with this catalogue: the LMC's field is a few-percent perturbation on the MW's, far below the 0.2 dex scatter of the sigma law, and the catalogue carries no sky positions -- the item is recorded as UNDERPOWERED, not as a null   (LMC term 33% of the MW's vs a 0.32 dex scatter; a detection would need sigma to ~2% per dwarf)

