====================================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  Item 8 does NOT close, and the failure is reported as found: with a stellar-population M/L the Local Group dwarfs sit 0.2-0.3 dex
  ABOVE the framework's EFE-quasi-Newtonian prediction, and centring needs Upsilon_V ~ 5-10.  This is a known MOND tension for MW
  dwarfs (Angus 2008), reproduced here rather than discovered, and it is a liability on the ledger, not a hit.  Two bugs were found
  and fixed in the making of it (the full baryonic mass used in a half-mass estimator; and the simple nu(x_ext) EFE prescription,
  which over-predicts DF2 by a factor 2 against the published careful calculation).  Item 42: the ultra-diffuse galaxies fall inside
  the framework's bracket only for DF2, which lands exactly on the Newtonian floor; DF4 sits below its own Newtonian floor and is
  a liability for every theory at the assumed M/L.  Item 96 is
  underpowered by two orders of magnitude and is recorded as such, not as a null.

